GZIP compression ->
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Purpose:
Reduces the size of a message by finding repeating patterns and replacing them with shorter codes,
effectively shrinking the data.

Algorithm:
Based on the DEFLATE algorithm, which combines LZ77 and Huffman coding.

Benefits:
Reduces bandwidth usage, speeds up data transfer, and can improve application performance by minimizing data size.

How it works:
Identifies and replaces repeating sequences of bytes with shorter codes.
Employs a dictionary to store these short codes and track their references throughout the data.
Utilizes Huffman coding to further compress the data, assigning shorter codes to more frequently appearing symbols.

Example in CPI:
The GZIP Encoder can be used to compress a message during an integration flow.

